<!--
    kuna `cmpmerge`: two comparisons of the same operands, combined by a
    boolean op or by two branches in a row to one target, often state one
    relation.  gcc -O0 compiles `a < b || a == b` as two branches, which
    print as `(a1 <= a0) && (a0 != a1)`; on doubles `a > b || a == b` and
    `a != b && !(a < b)` print as and-ands of two compares.  With the option
    on, each relation is a set of LT, EQ, GT and (floats) UN, and the pair
    folds into one comparison or its negation; floats keep the unordered
    outcome.  Default off: the merged forms move datatest assertions.

    Stage / sub-stage: P3 "simplification-quiescence", option
    `cmpmerge on|off`.

    The bytes are decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/cmpmerge.c
    built by gcc 15.3 at -O0 -fno-pie -no-pie -nostartfiles (x86-64).
    Pass 1 is the default (off), pass 2 `option cmpmerge on`.
-->
